<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==Description==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Inserts a subtractive cylinder in the active Body. Its shape is subtracted from the existing solid.
</div> 

[[File:PartDesign_SubtractiveCylinder_example.svg|none]]

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
''On the left: active body (A) shown in grey and subtractive cylinder (B) shown in transparent red; result on the right.''
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==Usage==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
# There are several ways to invoke the tool:
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:PartDesign_SubtractiveCylinder.svg|16px]] [[PartDesign_SubtractiveCylinder|Subtractive Cylinder]]}} button. '''Note''': the Subtractive Cylinder is part of an icon menu labelled ''Subtractive Primitive''. After launching FreeCAD, the Subtractive Box is the one displayed in the toolbar. To get to the Cylinder, click on the down arrow besides the visible icon and select Subtractive cylinder in the menu.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Part Design → Subtractive Primitive → [[Image:PartDesign_SubtractiveCylinder.svg|16px]] Subtractive Cylinder}} option from the menu.
# The task panel opens.
# Set the parameters. {{Version|26.3}}: If the {{MenuCommand|Show interactive draggers when editing features}} [[PartDesign_Preferences#General|preference]] is selected (default), some parameters can be adjusted with interactive gizmos in the [[3D_View|3D View]].
# Optionally set the [[Part_EditAttachment|Attachment]].
# Click {{Button|OK}}.
# A Cylinder feature appears under the active Body.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==Options==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
It is possible to create skewed cylinders by specifying angles in respect to the normal vector of the chosen attachment.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The Cylinder can be edited after its creation in two ways:
* Double-clicking it in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]], or by right-clicking and selecting '''Edit Primitive''' in the context menu; this brings up the task panel and ({{Version|26.3}}) the interactive gizmos (if enabled).
* Via the [[Property_View|Property View]].
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Operation ===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Sets the boolean operation used to combine the cylinder with the base solid. {{Version|26.3}}
* '''Subtraction''' (default): the cylinder removes its volume from the base solid, as in previous versions.
* '''Common''': the cylinder keeps only the volume shared between itself and the base solid, discarding everything else.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==Properties==
</div> 

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* {{PropertyData|Attachment}}: defines the attachment mode as well as the Attachment Offset. See [[Part_EditAttachment|Part EditAttachment]].
* {{PropertyData|Operation|Enumeration}}: sets the boolean operation used to combine the feature with the base solid (Subtraction, Common), see [[#Options|Options]]. {{Version|26.3}}
* {{PropertyData|Label}}: label given to the Cylinder object. Change to suit your needs.
* {{PropertyData|Radius}}: the radius value of the cylinder.
* {{PropertyData|Angle}}: angle of rotation of the cross section (360 degrees forms a full cylinder).
* {{PropertyData|Height}}: the height of the cylinder along its axis.
* {{PropertyData|First Angle}}: angle in first direction.
* {{PropertyData|Second Angle}}: angle in second direction.
</div>


